WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.001
[music playing]

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:03.903
 Eric, Jared, congratulations.

00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:05.739
Your weapons were strong
enough to propel you

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:08.441
into this final round of
competition, which means you're

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:10.877
both one step closer to the
title of "Forged in Fire"

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:13.880
champion and that
check for $10,000.

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:15.748
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:22.022
to create an iconic blade
from history, the Hunga Munga.

00:00:25.324 --> 00:00:28.728
The term Hunga Munga refers to
a variety of Central African

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.296
throwing knives,
all of which feature

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:33.465
a series of double-edged iron
blades attached to a rawhide

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:34.500
handle.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.235
The Hunga Munga was
not only formidable

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.538
in hand-to-hand combat but
could be thrown from a distance,

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.706
with some reports
claiming it had a throwing

00:00:40.806 --> 00:00:42.642
range of up to 250 feet.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:45.411
As armor was not used
often in Central Africa,

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:48.815
this type of throwing iron
was particularly devastating.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:50.916
Hunga Munga was
often very valuable

00:00:51.016 --> 00:00:52.418
and could be traded for goods.

00:00:52.484 --> 00:00:54.453
The Hunga Munga was
also wielded by Buffy

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:58.458
Summers in the cult series,
"Buffy the Vampire Slayer."

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:00.793
 First thing I
thought was [bleep]..

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:05.131
[laughs] I was not
expecting that.

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:08.134
 Your weapon must fall within
the following parameters.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:11.170
It must have a sharpened
head, crescent blade,

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:12.705
a spear, and a spike.

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:16.041
You must also include a handle
arm with a sharpened spike

00:01:16.141 --> 00:01:17.844
above the handle.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:21.380
It must be an effective, working
version of that deadly weapon.

00:01:21.447 --> 00:01:23.115
However, we want you
to make something

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:26.619
that's unique that could
only come from your forge.

00:01:26.685 --> 00:01:29.288 line:8%
 I'm looking forward to
decking this Hunga Munga out,

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:32.024 line:8%
and putting my own signature
style in the details

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:33.993 line:14%
and decorative work.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.361
 I'm trying to think
of how complicated

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:36.262
this thing will be to build.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.397
It's complicated forging.

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:40.132
 You will have five
days at your home

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.067
forge to complete
this challenge.

00:01:42.134 --> 00:01:43.436
At the end of those
five days, you

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:45.805
will return and present
your finished weapons

00:01:45.871 --> 00:01:47.707
to our panel of expert judges.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:50.175
Only after they've subjected
your weapons to a series

00:01:50.275 --> 00:01:53.445
of brutal tests will
they declare one of you

00:01:53.545 --> 00:01:55.948
the "Forged in Fire"
champion who walks away

00:01:56.014 --> 00:01:57.984
with that check for 10 grand.

00:01:58.084 --> 00:01:59.051
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:02.555
We'll see you in five days.

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:06.192 line:14%
[music playing]

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:11.230
 First day, really happy
to be back in my shop.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:15.835
I have never made anything
even remotely like this before.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:18.838
This is like a cross
between a sword,

00:02:18.904 --> 00:02:24.977
boomerang, chakram, battle axe.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:26.212
I gotta plan this out.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.580
I'm gonna start with
this blade, then

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.649
pull this off from
the side, and then

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:31.250
start working the spike in.

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.684
This is a wild build.

00:02:32.751 --> 00:02:34.354
[hammering]

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:36.623
[whirring]

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:39.358
JARED (VOICEOVER): So I'm
gonna have to heat this all up.

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:42.128
I'm gonna have to
drive this down.

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:43.596
 It's almost a chess game.

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.298
I've got to think like five
moves ahead on this thing,

00:02:45.364 --> 00:02:47.066
because if I screw
up once, it could

00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:48.734
completely ruin the
piece of steel I got

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:49.701
and I got to start over.

00:02:49.768 --> 00:02:51.171
[hammering]

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:55.841
This chunk here hopefully will
turn into my sickle blade here.

00:02:55.941 --> 00:02:56.943
[sawing]

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:01.013
Maybe if I heat this area here,
swinging this out of the way

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:01.814
here.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:02.682
[whirring]

00:03:03.582 --> 00:03:04.551
[hammering]

00:03:05.484 --> 00:03:07.319
I'm gonna push
that up into there.

00:03:07.419 --> 00:03:08.954
Then I can push this around.

00:03:09.021 --> 00:03:10.190
[whirring]

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:13.927
[hammering]

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:17.096
That's--

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:17.964
[clanging]

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:20.466
[inaudible] point's
going to be it.

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.835 line:14%
[music playing]

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:23.936 line:14%
[whirring]

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:25.138 line:8%
ERIC (VOICEOVER):
It's day three.

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:27.307 line:8%
I'm a little sore,
but I got the blade

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:31.844 line:8%
profiled, forged out, and feel
great about my blade design.

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:33.279
Bam.

00:03:33.346 --> 00:03:34.980
Still think it looks like
something from Whoville.

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:38.184
Now it's time for
the heat treat.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:40.486
Everything leading up to
this point is just critical.

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:41.454
[rumbling]

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:44.290
 All right, here we go.

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:51.197
Beautiful.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.398
[music playing]

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:53.699
ERIC (VOICEOVER):
I was totally giddy

00:03:53.799 --> 00:03:55.802
when I got it out of
the quench and I just

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.637
want to give it a test throw.

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:04.176
This thing is definitely
a lethal weapon.

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:06.312
It's not a prop.

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:08.780
It's definitely something
you don't want thrown at you.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:09.948
 It will stick.

00:04:10.015 --> 00:04:10.850
[laughs]

00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:12.851 line:14%
[music playing]

00:04:12.951 --> 00:04:14.453 line:8%
JARED (VOICEOVER): Plan for
today is finish up the pommel,

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.656 line:8%
carve in the sunbeam,
and then wrap the handle.

00:04:17.756 --> 00:04:20.393
This was a really difficult
piece to forge and to create.

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:26.198
Maybe I should have some worries
going into the final round,

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:28.367
but I really don't.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:29.602
I did the best I can do.

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:31.370
I'm super confident
in what I made.

00:04:31.436 --> 00:04:33.572
And just see how it pans out.

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:36.509
I think this thing's gonna
just perform spectacularly.

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:37.477
[scraping]

00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:41.447
My competitor-- he'd better
really bring his A-game,

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:43.116
because I'm feeling good.

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:46.386
 Bladesmiths, to see how
sharp your blades are,

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:49.255
I will take your weapon and I
will test the crescent-shaped

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:50.890
blade and the spear.

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:53.459
If your blade is sharp,
it should lacerate cleanly

00:04:53.525 --> 00:04:55.127
through this stretched leather.

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:55.961
Jared, you're up first.

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:56.728
Are you ready?

00:04:56.795 --> 00:04:57.597
 I am.

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:58.096
 Let's do this.

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:01.701
[music playing]

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.309
Well, Jared, your handle
wrap feels good to the hand.

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:13.212
The blade of your
crescent and your spear

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:16.215
right there is sharp
enough to lacerate cleanly

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:17.683
through the
stretched-out leather.

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:18.751
It will cut.

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:19.285
Good job, sir.

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:20.353
 Thank you.

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:21.153
 Eric, you're up.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:21.954
Ready?

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:22.955
 Yes, sir.

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:26.592
[music playing]

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:33.632
 OK, Eric.

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:34.800
Nice grip.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.637
Your crescent edge over
here, at the initial start,

00:05:37.704 --> 00:05:38.637
not so sharp.

00:05:38.737 --> 00:05:40.506
But once you got it
going, it lacerated.

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:42.408
Your spear edge, same thing.

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:43.575
It started off here.

00:05:43.642 --> 00:05:45.778
But once it got
going, it lacerated.

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:48.447
Not all edges are as
sharp as the other,

00:05:48.513 --> 00:05:50.450
but it is sharp enough to cut.

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:53.552
My concern was this design that
you have over here for this--

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:55.121
being that it's
a weapon that you

00:05:55.187 --> 00:05:59.124
move around, having that pointed
at me is never a good idea.

00:05:59.191 --> 00:06:00.392
 Right.

00:06:00.492 --> 00:06:03.262
 Otherwise, though,
this blade will cut.

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:03.996
Good job.

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:05.431
 Thanks.

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:08.267
ERIC (VOICEOVER): That
first slice skipped across

00:06:08.333 --> 00:06:10.970
and it got to a part
where it was sharper.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.471
Blade's not performing well.

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:14.406
I'm quite disappointed.

00:06:14.507 --> 00:06:16.876
 Bladesmiths, this
is a kill test.

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:19.578
The Hunga Munga was a weapon
with multiple configurations

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:21.614
of blades on top of a blade.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:24.717
To see how lethal your weapon
is according to its design,

00:06:24.784 --> 00:06:27.887
I will take your weapon and I
will deliver multiple strikes

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:29.354
on this ballistics dummy.

00:06:29.421 --> 00:06:31.123
Let's see how lethal
your blade is.

00:06:31.223 --> 00:06:32.058
Jared, you're up first.

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:32.791
You ready?

00:06:32.858 --> 00:06:33.325
 Definitely.

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:35.327
[music playing]

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:36.596
[squishing]

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:40.933
[squishing]

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:46.539
[squishing]

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:53.578
 [laughs] It looks
like he's bleeding.

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:56.916
 Well, Jared, every facet
and design of your blade

00:06:56.983 --> 00:06:58.484
will definitely do damage.

00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:02.421
Your crescent edge nicely
lacerated through the tip

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:05.758
on that hook and gutted
whatever was in there.

00:07:05.824 --> 00:07:07.460
For your small
blade, I had to angle

00:07:07.527 --> 00:07:09.529
a little bit because there's
not much space over there.

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:12.164
But, as you can see, if you
work it according to its design,

00:07:12.264 --> 00:07:13.765
you can jab right into it.

00:07:13.832 --> 00:07:16.235
And, of course, your spear
tip crushed through the bones

00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:17.135
and into the heart.

00:07:17.202 --> 00:07:19.672
This, sir, will kill.

00:07:19.739 --> 00:07:20.372
Great job.

00:07:20.439 --> 00:07:21.273
 Thank you.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:22.108
 Eric, you're up next.

00:07:22.208 --> 00:07:22.841
 Yes, sir.

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:23.375
 Let's do this.

00:07:23.476 --> 00:07:25.944
[music playing]

00:07:26.044 --> 00:07:27.079
[squishing]

00:07:29.047 --> 00:07:30.949
[crunching]

00:07:31.016 --> 00:07:31.984
[slapping]

00:07:35.721 --> 00:07:37.223
 Didn't get that
laceration there.

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:38.090
Hm.

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:38.924
 OK, Eric.

00:07:39.024 --> 00:07:40.659
Your spike right there?

00:07:40.726 --> 00:07:42.461
It's in a good
position because I

00:07:42.527 --> 00:07:45.164
can easily go in
there without worrying

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:47.066
about this getting in the way.

00:07:47.166 --> 00:07:48.667
So we come to the spear tip.

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:51.904
That went through all the way,
broke bone, and into the heart.

00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:53.739
Your weapon will kill.

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:54.406
Good job, sir.

00:07:54.473 --> 00:07:55.441
 Thank you.

00:07:55.507 --> 00:07:56.575
 Next up is the strength test.

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:58.544
For that, I'll pass
you on to Dave.

00:07:58.611 --> 00:08:00.979
 Gentlemen, we've seen that
the Hunga Munga can be used

00:08:01.046 --> 00:08:03.883
as a close-quartered weapon,
but it was specifically

00:08:03.983 --> 00:08:04.917
designed to be thrown.

00:08:05.017 --> 00:08:06.685
So to test the strength
of your weapon,

00:08:06.752 --> 00:08:08.987
I'm going to throw it three
times into our wooden target

00:08:09.054 --> 00:08:10.423
here.

00:08:10.523 --> 00:08:11.757
If your heat treat is sound,
the structural integrity

00:08:11.824 --> 00:08:13.892
of your weapon should
hold up to the impact.

00:08:13.959 --> 00:08:16.595
If not, we could have
a catastrophic failure.

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:17.996
Jared, you're up first.

00:08:18.063 --> 00:08:18.731
 Ready.

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:19.765
 All right.

00:08:19.865 --> 00:08:21.299
 Safeties.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:24.770
[music playing]

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:25.638
[tapping]

00:08:26.205 --> 00:08:27.773
ALL: Nice.

00:08:27.873 --> 00:08:28.407
 Damn.

00:08:28.473 --> 00:08:29.608
It split that log.

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:31.277
 [laughs] That's cool.

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:35.014
[clanging]

00:08:36.081 --> 00:08:36.849
 Ooh.

00:08:39.418 --> 00:08:41.020
 Nice.

00:08:41.087 --> 00:08:42.354
 No catastrophic failure.

00:08:42.421 --> 00:08:44.557
I'm happy it didn't break.

00:08:44.623 --> 00:08:46.926
 [grunts] [bleep]

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:51.330
 Nah, just a scratch.

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:52.397
 Boop.

00:08:52.497 --> 00:08:54.333
 Really happy with my design.

00:08:54.399 --> 00:08:56.135
Final throw, it
sticks in beautifully.

00:08:56.202 --> 00:08:58.470
 Well, as you can see,
this is a dangerous weapon

00:08:58.537 --> 00:08:59.672
all the way around.

00:08:59.739 --> 00:09:01.106
It feels really
good in the hand.

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:03.742
All that foward weight
makes it rotate beautifully.

00:09:03.809 --> 00:09:06.345
Your edge is still
a razor blade.

00:09:06.411 --> 00:09:07.913
I mean, once this
thing's traveling,

00:09:08.013 --> 00:09:09.515
I don't want to be on
the other side of it.

00:09:09.615 --> 00:09:12.585
Your cord wrap made it
really nice to throw.

00:09:12.652 --> 00:09:13.485
Well-executed.

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:14.286
 Thank you.

00:09:14.386 --> 00:09:16.188
 Eric, your turn.

00:09:16.255 --> 00:09:17.189
You ready?

00:09:17.256 --> 00:09:18.057
 Let's do it.

00:09:22.328 --> 00:09:23.228
[music playing]

00:09:23.328 --> 00:09:24.330
[bang]

00:09:29.468 --> 00:09:30.102
[thump]

00:09:30.202 --> 00:09:31.203
 Oh my.

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:36.975
 There you go.

00:09:37.075 --> 00:09:37.944
[bang]

00:09:38.343 --> 00:09:38.811
Nice.

00:09:43.782 --> 00:09:46.585
 Well, Eric, this feels
pretty good in the hand.

00:09:46.652 --> 00:09:48.721
I like all this detail
you did down in here.

00:09:48.787 --> 00:09:49.889
I mean, it doesn't
affect the throw.

00:09:49.955 --> 00:09:51.156
It doesn't affect the strength.

00:09:51.223 --> 00:09:52.524
But still, it's there.

00:09:52.625 --> 00:09:54.093
Dug in nicely.

00:09:54.159 --> 00:09:56.662
When I hit up here, it
kind of bounced out.

00:09:56.762 --> 00:09:57.830
It scored up the wood.

00:09:57.896 --> 00:09:59.365
It would have taken a man out.

00:09:59.465 --> 00:10:01.700
The other two throws
dug in nicely.

00:10:01.766 --> 00:10:03.735
Looks to me like your
edges held up fine.

00:10:03.802 --> 00:10:05.638
That's still all
right and tight.

00:10:05.704 --> 00:10:06.538
Nicely done, Eric.

00:10:06.605 --> 00:10:07.773
 Thank you.

00:10:07.873 --> 00:10:10.375
 Eric, Jared, you've
both done fantastic

00:10:10.442 --> 00:10:11.643
work on your Hunga Mungas.

00:10:11.743 --> 00:10:13.946
However, in this
arena of competition,

00:10:14.013 --> 00:10:16.414
there can only be one
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:10:16.515 --> 00:10:20.152
[music playing]

00:10:22.121 --> 00:10:23.655
Jared, congratulations.

00:10:23.722 --> 00:10:27.092
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:10:27.192 --> 00:10:30.396
Eric, your Hunga Munga
did not make the cut.

00:10:30.462 --> 00:10:31.730
Dave will explain.

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:34.299
 Eric, the addition of
that spike on the back

00:10:34.366 --> 00:10:35.667
was a question mark.

00:10:35.768 --> 00:10:37.703
But in the end, it came
down to the overall finish

00:10:37.803 --> 00:10:40.206
and construction and
the way it did not

00:10:40.272 --> 00:10:41.506
perform in the sharpness test.

00:10:41.606 --> 00:10:43.041
That's why we gotta let you go.

00:10:43.108 --> 00:10:46.979
 Eric, please surrender
your Hunga Munga.

00:10:47.046 --> 00:10:50.616 line:8%
ERIC (VOICEOVER): The judges'
feedback, I agree completely.

00:10:50.682 --> 00:10:52.317 line:14%
 I have no regrets whatsoever.

00:10:52.417 --> 00:10:54.252
ERIC (VOICEOVER): I came here
to prove that I could do it,

00:10:54.352 --> 00:10:58.424
that I could overcome a task
that was seemingly impossible.

00:10:58.524 --> 00:11:00.492
I may not be the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:11:00.558 --> 00:11:04.229
but I can only go up from here.

00:11:04.296 --> 00:11:05.631
 Jared, congratulations.

00:11:05.731 --> 00:11:07.967
You are our new "Forged in
Fire" champion and will be

00:11:08.033 --> 00:11:10.302
receiving a check for $10,000.

00:11:10.369 --> 00:11:11.436
How do you feel?

00:11:11.503 --> 00:11:12.738
[applause]

00:11:12.805 --> 00:11:15.241
 I don't know what
to say, really.

00:11:15.307 --> 00:11:16.975
It's kind of a shock right now.

00:11:17.075 --> 00:11:19.945
 That's straight-up
the prettiest

00:11:20.045 --> 00:11:22.915
and most terrifying thing
we've ever had on the show.

00:11:23.015 --> 00:11:23.915
 Thank you.

00:11:23.982 --> 00:11:25.217
 I mean, the
combination of the two.

00:11:25.284 --> 00:11:27.620
 I want it-- that's
how I feel about it.

00:11:27.687 --> 00:11:29.354
And I don't feel like that
about a lot of knives.

00:11:29.454 --> 00:11:31.356
But that's a cool piece.

00:11:31.423 --> 00:11:32.391
 Thank you.

00:11:32.458 --> 00:11:33.325
JARED (VOICEOVER): I won.

00:11:33.392 --> 00:11:34.626
Still kind of settling in.

00:11:34.693 --> 00:11:38.197
[laughs] 10 grand is
going into the shop.

00:11:38.263 --> 00:11:39.731
There'll probably be
a little trip involved

00:11:39.798 --> 00:11:41.767
for my fiance and myself.

00:11:41.834 --> 00:11:44.002
Boy, having the title of
"Forged in Fire" champion,

00:11:44.102 --> 00:11:48.174
it's going to definitely
be a game-changer.

